OL,3,AVolcano eruption leaves 150,000
OL,4,Apassengers stranded in Indonesia
OL,5,
OL,6,FMore than 150,000 passengers have been
OL,7,Fleft stranded after a volcanic eruption
OL,8,Fforced Indonesian authorities to
OL,9,Ftemporarily suspend operations at eight
OL,10,Fairports.
OL,12,FJakarta's Soekarno-Hatta International
OL,13,FAirport was the first to be closed on
OL,14,FSunday morning after ash from Anak
OL,15,FKrakatau was detected in airspace near
OL,16,Fthe airport.
OL,18,FTransport minister Dudy Purwagandhi
OL,19,Fsaid so far 712 flights have been
OL,20,Faffected and asked airlines to consider
OL,21,Fdiverting some flights to other
OL,22,Fairports.
OL,23,APub: 06-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/39
